{"id": "EUVD-2026-101226", "enisaUuid": "39660a71-77f1-3fae-b2b5-7fd029de18c0", "description": "Libyal libpff through 20260926 contains an integer underflow in libpff_record_entry_get_multi_value() that allows attackers to trigger heap out-of-bounds reads via non-monotonic multi-value offsets. Attackers can craft PST, OST or PAB files with decreasing PT_MV_STRING8, PT_MV_UNICODE or PT_MV_BINARY offsets to crash libpff, pypff or pffexport and expose adjacent heap memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:54:41", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libpff-multivalue-offset-underflow-oob-read", "https://github.com/libyal/libpff/blob/03545511ab7a7a609e50ec715bdd3985c3be71c5/libpff/libpff_record_entry.c#L2825-L2874", "https://github.com/libyal/libpff/blob/03545511ab7a7a609e50ec715bdd3985c3be71c5/libpff/libpff_multi_value.c#L207-L271", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libyal-libpff-through-20260926-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-libpff-record-entry-get-multi-value"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110598", "GHSA-9f2v-576g-7mp5"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7af60b14-d774-3c32-bb49-f7cbb7fe5ad5", "product": {"name": "libpff", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226420260926"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cd27813c-190b-35de-8fe2-8e949bed32b0", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}], "isExploited": false}